                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "756aaa79-1c83-3025-acf7-ed93fc6ac51b",
                                        "entry_id": "0dd3e362-ae72-3e59-8ef4-8dddf5a4c735",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be given, sent, or paid something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95792b75-b444-4cb0-896e-0f433993659a",
                                                "sense_id": "756aaa79-1c83-3025-acf7-ed93fc6ac51b",
                                                "text": "He received many presents for his birthday."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80c6b197-f48b-44d7-905b-581edb3f145d",
                                                "sense_id": "756aaa79-1c83-3025-acf7-ed93fc6ac51b",
                                                "text": "Nothing was too small to receive attention, if a supervising eye could suggest improvements likely to conduce to the common welfare. Mr. Gordon Burnage, for instance, personally visited dust-bins and back premises, accompanied by a sort of village bailiff, going his round like a commanding officer doing billets."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b49d0bf5-5b3c-4d93-88df-548f513271fd",
                                                "sense_id": "756aaa79-1c83-3025-acf7-ed93fc6ac51b",
                                                "text": "In America alone, people spent $170 billion on \"direct marketing\"—junk mail of both the physical and electronic varieties—last year. Yet of those who received unsolicited adverts through the post, only 3% bought anything as a result."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9d612ab9-9fec-3af2-8ca2-79f60ad27691",
                                        "entry_id": "0dd3e362-ae72-3e59-8ef4-8dddf5a4c735",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To take, as something that is offered; to accept."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aab29c8a-a4ac-4bb3-a85a-38b65fdd3f57",
                                                "sense_id": "9d612ab9-9fec-3af2-8ca2-79f60ad27691",
                                                "text": "He had the offer of employment, but he would not receive it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc3d4b9a-204d-4891-8de4-420728014f2c",
                                                "sense_id": "9d612ab9-9fec-3af2-8ca2-79f60ad27691",
                                                "text": "Our hearts receiue your warnings."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a981da0-c6fd-4b01-b336-2b1bae5fdd82",
                                                "sense_id": "9d612ab9-9fec-3af2-8ca2-79f60ad27691",
                                                "text": "The idea of solidity we receive by our touch."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5254ea09-d891-4498-90e5-364e690dac40",
                                                "sense_id": "9d612ab9-9fec-3af2-8ca2-79f60ad27691",
                                                "text": "[T]he braſen Altar that was before the Lord was too little to receiue the burnt offerings, and meat offerings, and the fat of the peace offerings."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d173b483-773e-49ae-be5f-41f1233ae683",
                                                "sense_id": "9d612ab9-9fec-3af2-8ca2-79f60ad27691",
                                                "text": "And afterwards Thou [God] receivedst Seth and Enoch, and Enoch Thou translatedst; for Thou art the Creator of men, the Fountain of Life, the Supplier of Want, the Giver of Laws, the Rewarder of them that keep them, the Avenger of them that transgress them."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd7ed6a7-f180-3329-9670-5107f1350d69",
                                        "entry_id": "0dd3e362-ae72-3e59-8ef4-8dddf5a4c735",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To take goods knowing them to be stolen."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9196365f-a0f0-3c6b-9848-dd1ff5107fe0",
                                        "entry_id": "0dd3e362-ae72-3e59-8ef4-8dddf5a4c735",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To act as a host for guests; to give admittance to; to permit to enter, as into one's house, presence, company, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff8292a8-b93d-42c8-9cb0-1839adf551e8",
                                                "sense_id": "9196365f-a0f0-3c6b-9848-dd1ff5107fe0",
                                                "text": "to receive a lodger, visitor, ambassador, messenger, etc."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ffc2c44b-f20d-486d-b3cd-321145788f58",
                                                "sense_id": "9196365f-a0f0-3c6b-9848-dd1ff5107fe0",
                                                "text": "And the barbarous people ſhewed vs no little kindneſſe: for they kindled a fire, and receiued us euery one becauſe of the preſent raine, and becauſe of the cold."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c1896ef-b56d-483a-be7f-336a2d49429b",
                                                "sense_id": "9196365f-a0f0-3c6b-9848-dd1ff5107fe0",
                                                "text": "In former days every tavern of repute kept such a room for the select circle—a club, or society, of habitués, who met every evening for a pipe and a cheerful glass. [...] Strangers might enter the room, but they were made to feel that they were there on sufferance; they were received with distance and suspicion."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0b8f995b-66ae-3e3c-87b1-ca27cb5f1f86",
                                        "entry_id": "0dd3e362-ae72-3e59-8ef4-8dddf5a4c735",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To incur (an injury)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b262318a-dd7c-43c9-9316-fbefbd5ae680",
                                                "sense_id": "0b8f995b-66ae-3e3c-87b1-ca27cb5f1f86",
                                                "text": "But because this is oftentimes dangerous, and much hurt hath been received thereby through casualty of fire, I advise the sticking four stakes into the earth, at least five feet above the ground [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34a5500d-0a58-4ff2-8a3b-f3f95530d2fd",
                                                "sense_id": "0b8f995b-66ae-3e3c-87b1-ca27cb5f1f86",
                                                "text": "I received a bloody nose from the collision."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d0c59210-c93b-3cd7-9f6a-de1193504540",
                                        "entry_id": "0dd3e362-ae72-3e59-8ef4-8dddf5a4c735",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To allow (a custom, tradition, etc.); to give credence or acceptance to."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46a74556-df7a-43d3-a536-72dc1371b43b",
                                                "sense_id": "d0c59210-c93b-3cd7-9f6a-de1193504540",
                                                "text": "For the Phariſes and all the Jewes, except they waſh their hands oft, eate not, holding the tradition of the elders. And when they come from the market, except they waſh, they eate not. And many other things there be, which they have receiued to hold, as the waſhing of cups and pots, braſen veſſels, and of tables."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d0731ad5-fc3e-316b-ba9f-6e88993b1df5",
                                        "entry_id": "0dd3e362-ae72-3e59-8ef4-8dddf5a4c735",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To detect a signal from a transmitter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "39e521ad-5f27-380b-8c79-127ff6fc525c",
                                        "entry_id": "0dd3e362-ae72-3e59-8ef4-8dddf5a4c735",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be in a position to take possession, or hit back the ball.",
                                            "To be in a position to hit back a service."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "14e1bacb-fc44-3d01-87bc-84d2adcd5371",
                                        "entry_id": "0dd3e362-ae72-3e59-8ef4-8dddf5a4c735",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be in a position to take possession, or hit back the ball.",
                                            "To be in a position to catch a forward pass."
